Z||000004||mshill||12-05-2001||10:00 AM||||Failing the NOx test would indicate something is wrong with the EGR ciruit.  The EGR valve may be new, and you won't get a code if you have vacuum at the solenoid, but there is no direct test to see if the solenoid is operating properly.  I put money on the solenoid.  <P>I used to get a code 32 after cruising at about 70 for 5-10 minutes.  Went to the pick-n-pull and got an EGR solenoid out of a Pontiac 6000 with a V6.  After turning the unit around in the bracket I stuck it in my 86SE and it passed smog with flying colors in October.||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroSTETZ||12-05-2001||12:05 PM||||hmmm- worth a try! will post the results!||||reg||1
