Z||000007||DRH||12-05-2001||12:21 PM||||I'm guessing here, but maybe the VSS really is the problem. Maybe the ECM only operates the EGR if it thinks the car is in motion?||||reg||1
Z||000008||Formula88||12-05-2001||03:15 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by yo_sweet:<BR><B>is it possible to pass the e-test with a exausht leak?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Not in the U.S.  That fails a visual inspection, if they notice it.||||reg||1
Z||000009||RedGTFieroKCMO||12-05-2001||09:53 PM||||I've heard that a new Converter has to be broken in first and be at operating temperature otherwise you might fail. Looks like you might want to check into this theory. Anyone else heard this before? ||||reg||5
Z||000010||California Kid||12-05-2001||10:19 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by RedGTFieroKCMO:<BR><B>I've heard that a new Converter has to be broken in first and be at operating temperature otherwise you might fail. Looks like you might want to check into this theory. Anyone else heard this before? </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I don't think that one is true, all cars have to meet emissions as part of the final line check at the assembly plant.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||FieroSTETZ||12-06-2001||04:28 PM||||okay, keep getting code 34- think its the egr solenoid, the only thing i have not replaced already. one question- there is a little tubey thing that used to stick out of the firewall side of the solenoid, and it looked like it went to the air canister. some time in the past, this rubber tube corroded or burned through, and now the tube is not there- could this cause the code? if it went to the air canister and the egr solenoid, could it be something that sucked dirty air and got plugged up? reading oliver scholz's page now to see if i can clean it out. <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.shawnrocks.com/Animation1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||terryk||12-06-2001||11:57 PM||||That tube from the EGR solenoid just went to the air cleaner so the EGR solenoid got fresh air. Not cosmic to the problem unless the port is plugged up. There is a little filter inside that cylindrical housing.<P>You can get that same solenoid from  billions of the MPFI cars in the junkyards.<P>It sounds like you aren't getting any EGR so the NOX are high.<P>What temp thermostat is in the car. You need to have the 195F in there.<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 12-07-2001).]||||reg||1
